# Deadweight — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. Nothing here is required: the site is fully usable with
# this file absent, because every figure on it comes from the deterministic
# engine and the letter from the warehouse has an engine-written version that
# ships when no model is reachable.
#
# Server-side only unless the name starts with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. Anything
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is compiled into the browser bundle — never put a key there.

# --- Google AI (the letter from the warehouse) -------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Without it, `POST /api/letter` answers with the engine's own letter and says
# so (`source: "engine"`, `refused: "unavailable"`). With it, a model writes the
# prose and the route throws the draft away unless every number in it is one the
# engine inserted.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Comma-separated, tried in order, first survivor wins. Defaults to
# `gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash`. Retiring an id is the
# failure mode these actually have, so it is config rather than a deploy —
# `gemini-2.5-flash` began answering 404 on 5 Sep 2026 while still being listed
# by the models endpoint, which is what this override is for.
# GEMINI_MODELS=gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash

# --- ElevenLabs (the letter, read aloud) -------------------------------------
# https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
# Without it, `POST /api/narrate` answers 503 and the panel reads the same words
# with the browser's own speech synthesis, saying which voice you are hearing.
# The voice model is only ever handed finished prose — it is given no figure to
# reason about and no opportunity to write one.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Optional, but recommended: with no voice pinned the route asks the account for
# one on every narration, which costs a round trip per request. Any voice id from
# https://elevenlabs.io/app/voices works.
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# Optional. Defaults to `eleven_multilingual_v2` — the docs call it the most
# stable on long-form generations and the better of them at speaking numbers,
# and this letter is long-form prose full of dollar amounts.
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_multilingual_v2

# --- The seal (which words the narration will read) --------------------------
# Optional. `/api/letter` seals every letter it emits, and `/api/narrate` reads a
# posted letter aloud only if the seal matches — otherwise it narrates the letter
# it computes from the same manifest, so an open endpoint never becomes a
# text-to-speech proxy funded by whoever owns the key above.
#
# Unset, the key is random per process: the seal holds within one instance, and
# across several the offer is dropped and the engine's letter is spoken instead.
# Set it — any long random string — and the seal holds across every instance and
# survives a redeploy, so a model-written letter is the one you hear.
# LETTER_SECRET=

# --- Solana (the devnet notary) ---------------------------------------------
# Optional. Devnet only — this layer notarises a verdict and moves no value.
# Defaults to the public devnet endpoint, which is rate-limited but adequate.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com
